 to advance  opportunities for research at least one  of the drugs David used in clinical  trials was later approved by the FDA  just in time to help hazel get through  some of her toughest moments did you  ever just get tired of going to the  hospital and tired of all these  treatments and tired of all the  medications yeah oh yeah and how did you  get through it all just by paying and  there is even more fighting ahead in  October hazel found out her cancer had  returned for the third time she's now on  a new drug in clinical trials the  doctors say he's promising thank you  this special soup the longer we can keep  a child like hazel here the research is  happening behind the scenes there's new  things coming out all the time and  there's so much exciting work being done  and so many advances but it has to be  fast enough you know to help hazel we  get to really enjoy everyday with each  other huh because we don't know what  tomorrow is gonna be thank you for the  opportunity to meet hazel what's really  sweet  two families one disease United in the  same fight cancer may rob a child of  their sense of invincibility to beat I  love you for CBS this morning Saturday  stay strong we counted Los Angeles
 

